hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27649","Haddathana Ishaq ibn Isa, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah informed me from Bukayr, from Busr ibn Sa'id, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, he said: Umar ibn al-Khattab disputed with me concerning the widow whose husband died while she is pregnant, so I said: She may marry when she delivers. Then Umm al-Tufayl, mother of my child, of Umar and mine, said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah to marry when she delivered."
"27650","Haddathana Yahya ibn Ishaq and Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, they both said: Haddathana Ibn Lahi'ah, from Bukayr ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Ashajj, from Busr ibn Sa'id, he said: I heard Umm al-Tufayl, Qutaybah said: wife of Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that she heard Umar ibn al-Khattab and Ubayy ibn Ka'b disputing. So Umm al-Tufayl said: Will not Umar ibn al-Khattab ask Subay'ah al-Aslamiyyah, whose husband died while she was pregnant, and she delivered after that by days, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, married her off?"
